Hmmm. You could try it a little differently.  They start as,
essentially, a normal humans (prehaps +1 STR/CON and -1 WIS/CHA).
Dragon alliegance depends upon alignment and/or class.  At level 3
they grow thier own set of dragon scales (of the appropriate colour).
When worn they work like normal dragon scale armour.  At level 7 or
so, they gain the ability to polymorph when they are wearing thier
scales, but only into a baby dragon of the corresponding colour.  At
level 14 they can polymorph into a full adult dragon.  (If we have
ancient dragons, they can poly morph into one of those at level 21.)
Note that the polymorph ONLY works with thier origial scales - if they
lose them or they are destroyed (or enchanted to become mail), they
lose the polymorph ability.

All dragons of thier same aliegance are generated friendly to them.

They get the canabalism penalty for eating a human or a dragon of the
same colour.  They also suffer a luck/alignment penalty for wearing
scale or mail from another dragon.  DragonSlayer swords always fight
them.

